[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: The library has three specific defects. First, FAIL_FAST at line 450 transitions both PENDING and READY nodes to CANCELLED, but the spec (dag_engine_lite.pyi line 432) mandates cancelling only PENDING nodes — READY nodes are eligible for execution and must not be cancelled. Second, retries_attempted at line 618 is set to attempt + 1, counting total executions rather than pure retry count — with retries=2 and max_attempts=3, the final attempt yields 3 instead of the spec-required 2 retries_attempted (dag_engine_lite.pyi line 129: 'Number of retries executed before final state'). Third, _sync_states() at line 365 resets all states whenever _current_nodes was never set (None from initialize), which destroys states manually set via mark_running/mark_failed — when is_finished() calls _sync_states() it wipes FAILED and SKIPPED states back to READY and PENDING, returning False instead of the spec-required True (dag_engine_lite.pyi line 446: 'When no ready nodes remain and unexecuted nodes are blocked by failed dependencies, MUST return True').
