[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: mark_running (lines 401-403) and mark_failed (lines 431-444) do not call _sync_states() before accessing or modifying self._states. When the test creates nodes via add_node (which only registers them in the DAG, not in _states) and then calls mark_running followed by mark_failed with FAIL_FAST, only f1 is in _states (set directly by mark_running). The FAIL_FAST loop at lines 442-444 iterates over _states.keys() which contains only f1, so PENDING nodes f3 and f4 are never cancelled. Per the spec (dag_engine_lite.pyi line 432), FAIL_FAST MUST transition all remaining PENDING nodes to CANCELLED, but since _sync_states() is not called, those nodes are never initialized in _states and the operation cannot fulfill its contract. Fix: add self._sync_states() at the start of both mark_running and mark_failed before any _states access, and similarly for mark_succeeded.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Added self._sync_states() at the start of mark_running, mark_succeeded, and mark_failed. This ensures all DAG nodes are initialized in _states (READY/PENDING) before any state mutations, so FAIL_FAST can correctly iterate over and cancel all PENDING nodes rather than only nodes that happen to be in _states from prior mark_running calls.
